# /tasks — Break Down the Plan into Tasks

Read the approved `specs/<feature>/plan.md` and write a detailed task
breakdown to `specs/<feature>/tasks.md`.

## Instructions

1. Confirm `specs/<feature>/plan.md` exists and is approved
   (`sddkit approve <feature> plan` must have been run).
2. Write `specs/<feature>/tasks.md` using the template below.
3. **Every REQ-NNN from the spec must be cited in at least one task.**
4. **Every task that involves new logic must include a corresponding test task.**
5. After writing, remind the user to run:
   ```
   sddkit check <feature>
   sddkit approve <feature> tasks
   ```

## tasks.md Template

```markdown
# Tasks: <Feature Name>

## Task List

- [ ] TASK-01: <title>  <!-- REQ-NNN -->
  - Description: ...
  - File(s): `src/...`
  - Done when: ...

- [ ] TASK-02: <title>  <!-- REQ-NNN -->
  - Description: ...
  - File(s): `src/...`
  - Done when: ...

- [ ] TASK-03: Write tests for <component>  <!-- REQ-NNN -->
  - Test file: `tests/test_....py`
  - Covers: REQ-NNN, REQ-NNN
  - Done when: all tests pass with `pytest`

## Definition of Done
- [ ] All tasks completed
- [ ] `sddkit check <feature>` exits 0
- [ ] All tests pass
- [ ] PR description links to spec
```

## Constraints
- Tasks must be small enough to complete in one session.
- Every REQ-NNN must appear in at least one task AND at least one test task.
- Do not begin implementation until all three stages are approved.
